  verse  and reports in the past have said that  marvel studios plans on bringing in the  midnight  suns and this is going to be sort of a  darker more adult  version of the mcu focusing on  characters like  moon knight blade dracula morbius and  the punisher right now as it stands and  appears to be seen marvel studios's plan  is to introduce a lot of different  teams to the marvel cinematic universe  and this is how they're going to  differentiate themselves from  the first four phases that we've had the  infinity saga because as it stands right  now  the future of the marvel cinematic  universe is going to have many different  teams it's going to have of course  the new avengers there's also going to  be a young avengers team  we know that we're getting the  thunderbolts and then we're going to be  getting the midnight suns as well but  let's not forget  about the x-men and the fantastic four  so as you can see there's going to be a  ton  of different groups coming to the marvel  cinematic universe all of which are  going to ultimately lead up to  a secret wars battleworld storyline and  not to mention  these are just the hero teams some of  them are anti-hero teams but  all are going to be used for the most  part to do good we haven't even talked  about the villains yet  with the x-men in the mcu comes magneto  in the mcu and there's a great chance  that he's going to establish his  brotherhood of evil  mutants bringing in some x-men  characters some evil mutants that we've  wanted to see in the mcu for a  very very long time now so as it stands  right now the future of the marvel  cinematic universe has never been  brighter and it's going to be much  bigger than the infinity saga  and there's going to be more than just  one storyline  in the first four phases everything kind  of intertwined with each other that's  the beauty of the marvel cinematic  universe  everything is connected and of course  everything is still going to be  connected in phase 5  6 7 and plus but the stories will be a  little bit  separate from each other with so many  teams it's going to have to be that way  you're going to have the x-men doing one  thing  the avengers doing another thing the  thunderbolts doing one thing and the  midnight sun's doing another  until eventually they all start coming  together and in the final  big showdown the avengers in-game level  event they'll all come together to form  a  massive superhero team which is  something that we're all  dying to see so for the next few phases  this is marvel's plan  establish a ton of different teams and  characters in the mcu  make incredible stories for them both in  the movies and  on disney plus and then eventually have  a villain or  villains so big like doctor doom and  galactus  come into play and threaten the earth  and universe to make  all of these different groups and heroes  come together for a final showdown  with them and this will be the event  that tops avengers end game and this is  what marvel studios plan  is right now so let me know how excited  you are about the next few years of the  marvel cinematic universe and let me  know what you think about the title  spider-man can't go home for spider-man  3. and also let me know your thoughts on  moon knight and  blade let me know what you think in the  comments down below don't forget to like  the video and subscribe  so you can stay up to date on all things  relating to the marvel cinematic  universe for live updates you can follow  me on twitter and as always thank you  all so much for watching  woof  you

